MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_001: Why, if it isn't Miss Alexandra! How fare you? One\ntoo rarely encounters a star twinkling in daytime.
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_002: I can see how a radiant beauty such as you earned\nthe nickname "Silver Maiden."
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_003: Heh. How kind, Sirocco. But I got that name only as\nleader of the Silver Knights of Tellus.
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_004: I didn't earn such a grand nickname. I have a lot to\nachieve before being truly worthy of it.
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_005: Hm. The compliment didn't resound with her. But\nsomehow that makes my fire burn all the more...
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_006: I understand this well! And I must say, it's refreshing\nto have my advances met with a cool breeze.
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_007: I don't believe I've sent any sort of weather your way.\nYou speak so colorfully, Sirocco.
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_008: Yes...well, thank you. Though to be clear, I'm not\nspeaking in jest!
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_009: My every breath is an expression of faith for Kalla,\nso with my words, I always try to be graceful.
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_010: I see... So it's temple talk? Spiritual devotion?
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_011: I'm so sorry! I had you completely wrong!
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_012: I'd gotten the idea that you're chasing pleasure.\nBut you're really after enlightenment!
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_013: Ah... Well. That may be overstating matters. But I\nappreciate you revising your opinion of me.
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_014: What do you think, Miss Alexandra? My schedule\nhappens to be uncharacteristically open this evening.
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_015: Having seen the sincerity in my heart, would you like\nto join me? Abandon ourselves to the night breeze?
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_016: What a wonderful idea! I'd like that, and I know\nthat Bucephalus would love to join us!
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_017: Bucephalus? Beg your pardon—who's this fellow?
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_018: My beloved steed! There's nothing more lovely than\nflying the evening winds with him.
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_019: Let's be off right away—before nightfall. Staying\nup too late isn't good for one's health!
MID_SE_Sci_Ale_C_020: She's too pure to be taken in by my charms.\nPerhaps we're both like the wind, in our ways...